# Brand-recreation themes: a palette is not a protected work, but a theme that recreates a real
# company's look is a statement this repo does not need to publish. A theme declares itself as one
# by writing `"note": "... reflecting <their site> ..."` (see harness/dev/preset-sheets.mjs and
# scripts/brand/*.mjs, which write themes this way); a human or agent adding a new brand-reflection
# theme must follow that convention so reviewers can find it by grepping `note` for "reflecting".
# `themes/presets/` is the one place this IS enforceable by path: every file there is a named
# reference-profile taste anchor (engine-doctrine/CRAFT/SELECTION.md), so the whole directory is ignored.
# Direct site recreations load by bare name (`themes/<name>.json`, see core/engine/boot.js /
# harness/author/treatment.mjs), so they cannot move under a subdirectory without a loader change;
# they stay listed here until one exists. They stay on disk so local brand work keeps rendering; they
# are not redistributed. The generic themes the templates use (default, northwind, neutral) are
# tracked and are what a fork should copy.
themes/presets/*.json
themes/stripe.json
themes/linear.json
themes/higgsfield.json

# Scratch experiment themes: one-off A/B variants (`ab*.json`) and per-person tryouts (`hi-<name>.json`)
# made for a single test render, never a shipped look. Pattern, not a filename list, so the next
# ab-run or hi-<name> experiment is ignored without a new line here.
themes/ab*.json
themes/hi-*.json

# scratch probe renders, written by hand during debugging and never an input to anything
assets/video/

# machine-specific Claude Code settings (never share)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Claude Code local config (agent-specific, not shipped): settings, plans, workflows
.claude/

# impeccable live-server local scratch
.impeccable/

# Uncredited capture assets, local-only (not shipped)
assets/rec1/
assets/rec3/

# Resource Boy gradient pack: no-redistribute licence, replaced by the gradient preset. Local-only.
assets/gradients/

# Ransom feature is local-only (Resource Boy licence): its demo scene html and sprites are not shipped
formats/scene/_ransom-intro-page.html
assets/ransom/

# site/public/blocklib/: `make previews` / `make preset-sheets` regenerate every mp4/png on demand
# (engine-doctrine/CRAFT/BLUEPRINTS.md, engine-doctrine/CRAFT/SELECTION.md), the same rule as out/**/*.mp4 above: a video
# instance is not the framework. The manifests (index.json) ARE committed, same as scenes-json's split.
site/public/blocklib/**/*.mp4
site/public/blocklib/**/*.png
!formats/scene/post-*.json
!formats/scene/post-*.storyboard.md
!formats/scene/post-*.html
!formats/scene/post-*.kit.css

# GENERATED MEDIA IS NOT SOURCE. mp3/wav/mp4/m4a files under out/ were tracked at various points,
# every one the output of a command in this repo; out/ is ignored wholesale above now, so nothing
# further is needed here. site/public/assets stays tracked: the marketing site SERVES those, so they
# are content.

# Per-brand demo imagery, the same rule assets/brands/** already applies, for two directories that
# predate it and escaped it. 4MB of one brand's hero art. The only scenes referencing them are
# untracked, so nothing tracked breaks.
assets/plinth/
assets/higgsfield/
